<h2 id="launch-plan">How to start a side hustle in Tampa this month</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Pick one gig and one area.</strong> A pressure washer in Carrollwood or a delivery zone in Brandon beats trying to cover all of Hillsborough County.</li>
  <li><strong>Register the basics.</strong> Check Hillsborough County and City of Tampa business tax receipt rules if you're offering services under your own name or brand.</li>
  <li><strong>Get listed where Tampa searches.</strong> Nextdoor, neighborhood Facebook groups, a free Google Business Profile and the apps for gig work.</li>
  <li><strong>Land three paying customers and ask for reviews.</strong> Photos and reviews matter more than ads in the first month.</li>
  <li><strong>Mark the calendar.</strong> Gasparilla, the State Fair, Bucs home games and hurricane season (June 1 to November 30) all shift demand.</li>
  <li><strong>Separate your money.</strong> Open a separate account, log mileage and set aside 25–30% of profit for taxes.</li>
</ol>
<div class="callout"><strong>Quick tip:</strong> Bundle services. A pressure-washing client is a likely lawn or pool customer, and a co-host who likes your cleaning will refer three more hosts. Ask every happy customer what else they need.</div>

<h2 id="florida-rules">Florida taxes and Tampa rules</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>No state income tax:</strong> Florida doesn't tax personal income, so you won't file a state return for side income.</li>
  <li><strong>Federal taxes:</strong> you owe income tax plus 15.3% self-employment tax on net profit. Use our <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a> and make quarterly payments once you expect to owe $1,000 or more.</li>
  <li><strong>Local business tax receipts:</strong> Hillsborough County requires a local business tax receipt, and businesses within Tampa city limits need a City of Tampa receipt as well.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax:</strong> product sellers register with the Florida Department of Revenue and collect the 6% state rate plus the county surtax.</li>
  <li><strong>Short-term rentals:</strong> hosts owe the state transient rental tax and Hillsborough County's tourist development tax unless the platform remits them. Unincorporated Hillsborough has adopted a vacation rental registration program, so confirm the current rules for your address.</li>
</ul>

